{"schema_version":"1.8.0","id":"JLSEC-2026-1175","published":"2026-08-07T13:27:45.313Z","modified":"2026-08-08T23:15:04.277047669Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-64833","GHSA-34g6-m4cp-w5c9","EUVD-2026-47757"],"summary":"FFmpeg versions 0.7.1 through 8.1.2 contain an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the S/PDIF...","details":"FFmpeg versions 0.7.1 through 8.1.2 contain an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the S/PDIF muxer that allows attackers to access memory beyond buffer boundaries by supplying a crafted DTS stream with a `core_size` value larger than the actual packet length. Attackers can exploit the missing bounds check in the `spdif_header_dts4` function by providing a malicious DTS-HD audio stream during S/PDIF re-muxing to trigger unauthorized memory reads beyond the packet buffer.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"FFMPEG_jll","ecosystem":"Julia","purl":"pkg:julia/FFMPEG_jll?uuid=b22a6f82-2f65-5046-a5b2-351ab43fb4e5"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"9.0.0+0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/JuliaLang/SecurityAdvisories.jl/tree/generated/osv/2026/JLSEC-2026-1175.json"}},{"package":{"name":"FFMPEG_nogpl_jll","ecosystem":"Julia","purl":"pkg:julia/FFMPEG_nogpl_jll?uuid=a6892c6b-5768-548c-b024-ff8dabf482c5"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"9.0.0+0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/JuliaLang/SecurityAdvisories.jl/tree/generated/osv/2026/JLSEC-2026-1175.json"}},{"package":{"name":"FFplay_jll","ecosystem":"Julia","purl":"pkg:julia/FFplay_jll?uuid=c4dce911-e170-5107-8314-c7bdc6785395"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"9.0.0+0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/JuliaLang/SecurityAdvisories.jl/tree/generated/osv/2026/JLSEC-2026-1175.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/6f80e2765492700622596af720534cef33dd31b4"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg